<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Flag Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Black Flags</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Flag Army was a band of Chinese irregulars led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-yongfu">Liu Yongfu</a>, formed from rebel remnants who crossed into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the 1860s. Taken into the service of the Vietnamese court, it controlled trade on the Red River and fought the French in Tonkin, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-garnier">Francis Garnier</a> in 1873 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-riviere">Henri Rivière</a> in 1883. It fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a> and was disbanded after the peace of 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-flag-army.jpg" alt="Black Flag Army" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Djwilms. The original uploader was Djwilms at English Wikipedia.; derivative work by xavax · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Flag_Army_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
